# Firebase project identifiers for the phone build.
#
# COMMITTED ON PURPOSE, and it is worth saying why in a public repo.
#
# These four values are compiled into the app and are readable by anyone who
# unzips the APK — Google's own documentation says google-services.json is not
# a secret for exactly that reason. Keeping them out of the repo would hide
# them from nobody and would stop CI building a push-enabled app at all.
#
# WHAT IS SECRET is the service-account key, which authorises SENDING. It lives
# outside both repos entirely, and is named in backend/.env. It must never
# appear here.
#
# Worth doing once in the Google Cloud console: restrict this API key to the
# Android package name and the iOS bundle id, so it is useless anywhere else.
#
# FCM_API_KEY_IOS is absent until GoogleService-Info.plist is supplied, so an
# iPhone build has no push yet. Android is complete.
FCM_API_KEY_ANDROID=AIzaSyAHRRfK4z1VNa21Rxb17EuupGnYmZ5Q36k
FCM_APP_ID_ANDROID=1:527918334515:android:213378d0e5fc39684a5946
FCM_APP_ID_IOS=1:527918334515:ios:3781144c60434bef4a5946
FCM_PROJECT_ID=safenest-dd21f
FCM_SENDER_ID=527918334515
